  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Jack Setton helped turn high-fidelity sound into a mass-market aspiration through advertising that reached beyond specialist magazines. One campaign paired a pulsing loudspeaker with a heartbeat; another transformed the Arc de Triomphe into a sound system. He also launched equipment under his own name, coordinating French design with Japanese production.\n\nHis Association Setton supplied sleeping bags to people without homes. His mother, Lili, developed the idea after meeting a man whose cardboard shelter had been stolen, then organised distribution through charities. Pioneer provided office space and administrative support. After her death, the association renamed its sleeping bag Le Lili.",
    "html": "<p>Jack Setton helped turn high-fidelity sound into a mass-market aspiration through advertising that reached beyond specialist magazines. One campaign paired a pulsing loudspeaker with a heartbeat; another transformed the Arc de Triomphe into a sound system. He also launched equipment under his own name, coordinating French design with Japanese production.</p>\r\n<p>His Association Setton supplied sleeping bags to people without homes. His mother, Lili, developed the idea after meeting a man whose cardboard shelter had been stolen, then organised distribution through charities. Pioneer provided office space and administrative support. After her death, the association renamed its sleeping bag Le Lili.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 99,
